# Tests

## Layout

- API feature tests: `tests/Feature/v1/{Domain}/` (e.g. `Question/QuestionsTest.php`)
- Namespace matches folder: `Feature\v1\{Domain}` (see existing tests)
- Extend `Tests\TestCase`

## Database

Use `Illuminate\Foundation\Testing\DatabaseTransactions` — **not** `RefreshDatabase`:

```php
class QuestionsTest extends TestCase
{
    use DatabaseTransactions, WithUser;
}
```

PHPUnit uses SQLite in-memory (`phpunit.xml`). Clean specific tables in `setUp()` only when the test requires an empty slate (e.g. `DB::table('questions')->delete()`).

## Auth & permissions

- `App\Traits\Tests\WithUser` — `getUser()` creates a user with `$this->permission`
- Set `protected string $permission = 'view-any-question';` (or relevant ability) per test class
- Assert `assertForbidden()` / `assertOk()` against named routes: `route('api.v1.questions.list')`

## Structure

- One test class per endpoint group or feature area
- Method names: `test_{actor}_{condition}_{expected}` (snake_case, readable)
- Use factories (`Question::factory()`, `User::factory()`) and `actingAs()`
- Prefer `getJson` / `postJson` for API tests
- Assert resource payloads under `data.*` (e.g. `assertJsonPath('data.delta', 1)`), not at the JSON root

## What to cover

- Permission gates (with and without ability)
- Happy path + validation errors (`assertUnprocessable`, `assertJsonValidationErrors`)
- Domain-specific edge cases (filters, soft deletes, status transitions)

Do not add trivial unit tests that only assert framework behavior unless requested.
